From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: strain08 <strain08@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] freebsd: match remote-server name to install-server

A stable/preview client builds the remote-server filename it looks for
from version.to_string(), which includes semver build metadata such as
"1.5.3+stable.<sha>" (the commit sha is injected by crates/zed/build.rs).
That never matches the name script/freebsd-patches install-server writes
(zed-remote-server-stable-1.5.3), so the on-host binary check fails and
the client falls back to fetching a FreeBSD release that does not exist,
surfacing as: failed to fetch release: "bad request. Need `asset`, `os`,
`arch`".

Strip pre-release/build metadata when forming the name, mirroring the
normalization auto_update already applies in get_release_asset. The
expected binary becomes zed-remote-server-<channel>-<version>, which is
stable across rebuilds and matches the install-server output.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/remote/src/transport/ssh.rs | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/crates/remote/src/transport/ssh.rs b/crates/remote/src/transport/ssh.rs
index 2beae54f2f..a628e666f0 100644
--- a/crates/remote/src/transport/ssh.rs
+++ b/crates/remote/src/transport/ssh.rs
@@ -794,7 +794,17 @@ impl SshRemoteConnection {
     ) -> Result<Arc<RelPath>> {
         let version_str = match release_channel {
             ReleaseChannel::Dev => "build".to_string(),
-            _ => version.to_string(),
+            _ => {
+                // Strip pre-release/build metadata (e.g. "+stable.<sha>") so the
+                // on-disk server name is "zed-remote-server-<channel>-<version>",
+                // matching what `script/freebsd-patches install-server` produces and
+                // staying stable across client rebuilds. Mirrors the normalization
+                // already done in auto_update's get_release_asset.
+                let mut version = version.clone();
+                version.pre = semver::Prerelease::EMPTY;
+                version.build = semver::BuildMetadata::EMPTY;
+                version.to_string()
+            }
         };
         let binary_name = format!(
             "zed-remote-server-{}-{}{}",
